Chapter: FactLog

 We say:

Section: Sizes And Offsets

 A 512-byte sector; the fact log starts at sector 2; the entry header is
 78 bytes -- a 32-byte content hash, then a 2-byte kind, a 32-byte gap, an
 8-byte timestamp, and a 4-byte content length -- and the content follows.
 The superblock holds an 8-byte magic, then the log head at offset 8 and
 the generation counter at offset 24. Kind 30 is a source definition.

  fl-sector-size : Integer = 512
  fl-fact-log-start : Integer = 2
  fl-header-size : Integer = 78
  fl-magic : Text = "CODEXFS1"
  fl-kind-definition : Integer = 30

  fl-off-kind : Integer = 32
  fl-off-timestamp : Integer = 66
  fl-off-content-len : Integer = 74
  fl-off-sb-log-head : Integer = 8
  fl-off-sb-index-gen : Integer = 24

Section: Little-Endian Reads

  fl-u16 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fl-u16 (buf) (off) =
   bit-or (peek-byte buf off) (bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 1)) 8)

  fl-u32 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fl-u32 (buf) (off) =
   let b0 = peek-byte buf off
   in let b1 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 1)) 8
   in let b2 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 2)) 16
   in let b3 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 3)) 24
   in bit-or b0 (bit-or b1 (bit-or b2 b3))

  fl-u64 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fl-u64 (buf) (off) =
   let b0 = peek-byte buf off
   in let b1 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 1)) 8
   in let b2 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 2)) 16
   in let b3 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 3)) 24
   in let b4 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 4)) 32
   in let b5 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 5)) 40
   in let b6 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 6)) 48
   in let b7 = bit-shl (peek-byte buf (off + 7)) 56
   in bit-or b0 (bit-or b1 (bit-or b2 (bit-or b3 (bit-or b4 (bit-or b5 (bit-or b6 b7))))))

 A run of bytes read back as CCE text, one code point per byte, exactly as
 it was packed. The accumulation is quadratic in the run length; a work is
 a few kilobytes, and this is not a hot path.

  fl-text : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  fl-text (buf) (off) (len) = fl-text-loop buf off len 0 ""

  fl-text-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  fl-text-loop (buf) (off) (len) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else let ch = char-to-text (code-to-char (peek-byte buf (off + i)))
   in fl-text-loop buf off len (i + 1) (acc & ch)

Section: Derived

  fl-sectors-for : Integer -> Integer
  fl-sectors-for (content-len) =
   (fl-header-size + content-len + fl-sector-size - 1) / fl-sector-size

Section: Reading A Field From A Sector Buffer

  fl-magic-ok : Integer -> Boolean
  fl-magic-ok (buf) = fl-text buf 0 8 == fl-magic

  fl-entry-kind : Integer -> Integer
  fl-entry-kind (buf) = fl-u16 buf fl-off-kind

  fl-entry-timestamp : Integer -> Integer
  fl-entry-timestamp (buf) = fl-u64 buf fl-off-timestamp

  fl-entry-content-len : Integer -> Integer
  fl-entry-content-len (buf) = fl-u32 buf fl-off-content-len

  fl-sb-log-head : Integer -> Integer
  fl-sb-log-head (buf) = fl-u64 buf fl-off-sb-log-head

  fl-sb-index-gen : Integer -> Integer
  fl-sb-index-gen (buf) = fl-u64 buf fl-off-sb-index-gen
